{
  "translate_en|mods/TheZims/42/media/lua/shared/Translate/EN/IG_UI.json|IGUI_TheZims_AboutBody": "The Zims is the base. On its own it draws nothing in the world: what it brings is the frame every expansion plugs into - the drawing library, the theme, the 3D portrait and this window.|#How to use|Pick an expansion in the menu on the left. Each one tells you what it does, whether you have it, and gives you a switch to turn it on or off without touching the mod list or restarting.|Cards shown in solid blue are still being built. They are there so you can see what is coming; there is nothing to open inside them yet.|#One family, one look|Every piece is its own mod, updated on its own. The base keeps them looking like one thing: same colours, same rounded shapes, one window and one key.|#Controller|Point the stick at an option and it lights up: the wheel reads the angle you are aiming at, the way a weapon wheel does. A confirms, B goes back a level, LB and RB turn the page. A direction only moves the highlight, it never confirms. Your survivor stands still while the wheel is open.|#Compatibility|Tested alongside the NeatUI family with no conflicts. Nothing here replaces game systems: The Zims draws, it does not rewrite. If you hit a conflict with any mod, please report it - silent breakage is the one thing that cannot be fixed.|#What is coming|Animations on the pieces that open and close. Zim Panel, the status HUD with the 3D portrait, need bars, moodles and body condition. Zim Bath, a real bath in a bathtub. And more after those.",
